        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: શોખ",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "શોખ — śokh — \"hobby, keen interest\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "મારા દાદાને ગાવાનો શોખ હતો. — mārā dādāne gāvāno śokh hato — \"My grandfather was fond of singing.\""
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "શોખ (śokh) is a loan from Arabic shawq, \"longing, desire\", which reached Gujarati through Persian. Its Arabic root is sh-w-q (Lane)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
